# ── CWRU dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Committed so the project runs on another machine without a separate
# download. Only the 64 recordings the project actually uses are kept:
# ingestion/manifest.py takes 12k_DE + Normal and skips 12k_FE / 48k_DE, so
# that is 60 drive-end recordings + 4 Normal, ~186 MB. The rest stays local.
# (Git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded folder, so each level
# excludes its *contents* and re-includes only the path that leads down.)
data/raw/*
!data/raw/cwru/
data/raw/cwru/*
!data/raw/cwru/CWRU_organized/
data/raw/cwru/CWRU_organized/*
!data/raw/cwru/CWRU_organized/12k_DE/
!data/raw/cwru/CWRU_organized/Normal/
*.zip
*.mat
!data/raw/cwru/CWRU_organized/12k_DE/**/*.mat
!data/raw/cwru/CWRU_organized/Normal/**/*.mat

# ── Generated output ─────────────────────────────────────
eda_output/
# ML output stays local, EXCEPT the files the running app reads: the four
# deployed checkpoints (pipeline.py silently skips a site with no checkpoint,
# so a fresh clone would replay nothing) with their metrics, and the federated
# summary the dashboard plots. Retraining elsewhere would not reproduce them --
# ml/train.py saves the last epoch, and every documented figure is from these.
/mlruns/
backend/mlruns/*
!backend/mlruns/depot_1/
!backend/mlruns/depot_2/
!backend/mlruns/depot_3/
!backend/mlruns/depot_4/
backend/mlruns/depot_*/*
!backend/mlruns/depot_*/cnn_state_dict.pt
!backend/mlruns/depot_*/metrics.json
!backend/mlruns/federated/
backend/mlruns/federated/*
!backend/mlruns/federated/fedprox/
backend/mlruns/federated/fedprox/*
!backend/mlruns/federated/fedprox/federated.json

# ── Local databases ──────────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.sqlite

